    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), whose matchup against S. Lugo provides the day\u2019s premier combination of power and table-setting upside. With favorable park factors and a strong platoon advantage, **Gunnar Henderson** is poised to anchor the offense. Close behind is **Kyle Tucker** (75.19), who remains an elite start despite the standard platoon considerations; his raw talent against Bratt allows him to transcend matchup constraints. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (74.07) benefits significantly from facing a softer arm in Schultz, yielding a high-efficiency score that underscores his role as a staple in our daily rotation. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.69) and **Andy Pages** (72.56) also find themselves in excellent positions to capitalize on suspect opposing pitching, providing the necessary depth to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 landscape.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today was **Brayan Rocchio** (59.25), who narrowly missed the cut. While his efficiency score is robust, the optimizer favored the higher-upside matchups held by **Sam Antonacci** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose platoon advantages and lineup positions provided a more reliable path to offensive production. We continue to monitor the risk profile of **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**; while their scores of 62.77 and 63.85 respectively make them solid starts, they are facing pitchers who historically struggle to control the running game. Given our organizational priority on stolen bases, the \"Slow SP Delivery\" tags for both opposing pitchers offer a hidden value boost that justifies their inclusion, as we look to manufacture extra value in an otherwise scarce category. The lineup remains settled, though owners should keep an eye on the wind conditions affecting **Drake Baldwin**, whose score took a slight dip due to the unfavorable wind-in forecast.",
